  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "After migration, it is impossible to update/delete triples from a 4.7.x repository that used language-tagged strings created in 4.6.x.  Moreover, any SPARQL Update request that attempts to delete an affected triple, but which may attempt to update/delete other triples for the same resource, will fail.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "(I'm assuming all versions of 4.6 and 4.7 are an issue here, but I've only confirmed 4.6.1->4.7.0 and 4.6.1->4.7.4.)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Two different behaviors have been observed depending on whether you are trying to delete one of these triples from 4.7.0 versus 4.7.4.  ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "4.7.0: PATCH response returns \"400 Bad Request\" and the response body will include a message like \"Property 'ns001:prefLabel': Unable to remove value 'Hello^^http:....\"",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "4.7.4: PATCH response returns \"204 Content Updated.\"  But the triple remains.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This gist should reproduce the issue sufficiently: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://gist.github.com/kefo/3272ec4fa07da7ab9855db843922b295"
         },
